DirkuLator 0.60rc: the game's music is not played. A voice that loops a wave buffer for ever (loop_count < 0)
is still decoded, so its state and timing are unchanged, but its output is silenced. Ambient loops go with it.
EDEN_MUSIC_MUTED logs the first and every doubling of voice updates silenced. /data/eden-nx2/music-on.txt
(main.cpp sets EDEN_NX2_MUSIC_ON) plays the music again.

diff --git a/src/audio_core/renderer/command/data_source/decode.cpp b/src/audio_core/renderer/command/data_source/decode.cpp
--- a/src/audio_core/renderer/command/data_source/decode.cpp
+++ b/src/audio_core/renderer/command/data_source/decode.cpp
@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@
 #include <atomic>
 #include <chrono>
 #include <cstdio>
+#include <cstdlib>
+#include <cstring>
 #include <vector>
 
 #include "audio_core/renderer/command/data_source/decode.h"
@@ -268,6 +270,14 @@
         }
     }
 #endif
+#ifdef EDEN_NX2_PS5_PROTO
